+Concise Bounded Description
+---------------------------
+
+To extract the description of a single resource from a graph, use
+:meth:`~rdflib.graph.Graph.cbd`. It returns a new ``Graph`` holding the
+Concise Bounded Description (CBD) of the resource, as defined in the
+`W3C member submission <https://www.w3.org/Submission/CBD/>`_: every
+triple whose subject is the resource, plus, recursively, the triples of
+any blank node objects reached along the way::
+
+    >>> from rdflib import Graph, URIRef, Literal, BNode
+    >>> g = Graph()
+    >>> alice = URIRef("http://example.org/alice")
+    >>> address = BNode()
+    >>> g.add((alice, URIRef("http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name"), Literal("Alice")))
+    >>> g.add((alice, URIRef("http://example.org/address"), address))
+    >>> g.add((address, URIRef("http://example.org/city"), Literal("Paris")))
+    >>> len(g.cbd(alice))
+    3
+
